2025-12-29 03:53:50 - Agent_20251229035223 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed CodeQL race condition findings in cachetools cache decorator functions. Identified and submitted 2 confirmed true positive vulnerabilities:

1. Race condition in _locked_info function (line 50-67): The function checks cache under lock, releases it, calls the wrapped function, then re-acquires lock. This creates a window where multiple threads can compute the same value simultaneously.

2. Race condition in _locked function (line 169-184): Similar pattern with cache check under lock, lock release, function call, and lock re-acquisition, allowing concurrent computation of the same cached values.

Both vulnerabilities are confirmed race conditions (CWE-362) where multi-threaded access to cache operations is not properly synchronized throughout the entire critical section. While setdefault() provides some mitigation by preferring already-cached values, it doesn't prevent the redundant computation and potential performance/resource issues from multiple threads executing the same expensive function.
